  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nAs a strong low pressure system slowly exits east through NE \nMontana widespread rain showers with embedded isolated \nthunderstorms, mostly though the early hours of the morning on\nThursday. A strong cold front will sweep down from Saskatchewan \ngenerating rain Thursday with wet snow at highest elevations such\nas Opheim. Brief, heavy snow is also possible through mid morning\nwhich could impact the morning commute and put significant strain\non newborn livestock. This prompted a Winter Weather Advisory for\nnorthern Valley county through the morning. Gusty winds will also\npersist through the day with northwest gusts 30-50 mph. A High \nWind Warning was raised Thursday until 8pm across the area for \noccasional gusts to around 60 mph being likely and pockets of \n40 mph sustained winds. \n\nMuch cooler weather looks to stick around through next week, with\nlows to stay at or below freezing through the forecast cycle. An \nadditional shortwave passing through Friday presents a chance for \nmore widespread snow showers. Gusty winds continue through \nFriday's system as well. \nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nBlended in 25% NBM90 for day 1 wind gusts. Used a blend of HiRes\nmodels for PoPs through 3Z tomorrow. Added more widespread showers\nthrough 18Z.",
